  "comment": "Why: the vampire court is a household: thralls on the stair, hounds in the yard, bats in the belfry, gargoyles on the roof, and above them the nobles, who are few and hard. The table puts the household in front (bats, thralls, wolves) and keeps the lord for the hard band; the belfry swarm answers noise, the hunt answers noise too, and a few entries wait for the dark because a castle that is lit for guests is a castle at rest. The danger is high (a hungry court), so the roll bonus is one.",
